$CATEGORY: Q4 - VARIABLES

::Q401::
variable - A named storage location for values. All variables have a type which is declared when the variable is created.{TRUE}

::Q402::
value -    A number, string, or other data that can be stored in a variable. Every value belongs to a type (e.g., int or String).{TRUE}

::Q403::
type -    A set of values. The type of a variable determines which values it can have.{TRUE}

::Q404::
You can use keywords (like public, class, and void) as variable names.{FALSE}

::Q405::declaration{
    =A statement that creates a new variable and specifies its type
    ~A statement that gives a value to a variable.
    ~To assign a variable for the first time.
}

::Q406::assignment{
    ~A statement that creates a new variable and specifies its type
    =A statement that gives a value to a variable.
    ~To assign a variable for the first time.
}

::Q407::initialize{
    ~A statement that creates a new variable and specifies its type
    ~A statement that gives a value to a variable.
    =To assign a variable for the first time.
}
    
$CATEGORY: Q5 - OPERATIONS

::Q501::operator{
    =A symbol that represents a computation like addition, multiplication, or string concatenation.
    ~One of the values on which an operator operates. Most operators in Java require two operands
}

::Q502::operand{
    ~A symbol that represents a computation like addition, multiplication, or string concatenation.
    =One of the values on which an operator operates. Most operators in Java require two operands
}

::Q503::
expression -    A combination of variables, operators, and values that represents multiple values. {FALSE}

::Q506::
concatenate -   To join two values, often strings, end to end.{TRUE}

::Q507::
order of operations - The rules that determine in what order expressions are evaluated.{TRUE}

$CATEGORY: Q6 - ERRORS

::Q601:: compile-time error{
    =An error in the source code that makes it impossible to compile. Also called a “syntax error”
    ~An error in a program that makes it impossible to run to completion. Also called an “exception”
    ~An error in a program that makes it do something other than what the programmer intended.
}

::Q602::
floating-point - A data type that represents numbers with an integer part and a fractional part. 
    In Java, the default floating-point type is double.{TRUE}

::Q603::
rounding error - The difference between the number we want to represent 
    and the nearest floating-point number.{TRUE}

::Q604:: run-time error{
    ~An error in the source code that makes it impossible to compile. Also called a “syntax error”
    =An error in a program that makes it impossible to run to completion. Also called an “exception”
    ~An error in a program that makes it do something other than what the programmer intended.
}

::Q605::logic error{
    ~An error in the source code that makes it impossible to compile. Also called a “syntax error”
    ~An error in a program that makes it impossible to run to completion. Also called an “exception”
    =An error in a program that makes it do something other than what the programmer intended.
}
